 "cfo_summary": [
  "<strong>Total available cash is $90,683</strong> against a true bank balance of $148,696. After <strong>$5,757 in external payments</strong> and <strong>$45,000 in intercompany distributions</strong>, projected end of week is <strong>$84,926</strong>. Seventeen bills, but only six are external. The month's park distributions to Group Group make up 89 percent of the run.",
  "<strong>GRP is overdrawn at the bank.</strong> True bank is negative $8,344, the first negative true balance in fifteen weeks. Available is negative $51,072 with $42,728 of uncleared items on top. GRP has fallen from $34,280 on 8/7 to $3,970 on 8/14 to negative $8,344 today, a $42,624 decline in two weeks against only $24,299 of payables in that period. The difference cleared outside the payables template and needs identifying.",
  "<strong>Group Group is funded for the first time in months.</strong> The seven park distributions totaling $45,000 land this week, taking GG from $87 to a projected $45,087. Tim's withdrawal typically follows in week three, so this money is expected to leave again shortly.",
  "<strong>Decade Acres projects to $569 and Riverside to $2,345</strong> after their distributions. Four Seasons falls to $4,099 and Country Aire to $9,260. Countryside at $67,717 is the only entity with meaningful capacity and remains the sole funding source for GRP.",
  "<strong>The forecast goes negative in three of nine weeks</strong>, bottoming at negative $56,976 on 10/16. This is a change in the base, not a change in the business. Opening cash has dropped $170,406 in two weeks as the uncleared backlog settled, so the forecast now runs from real cash rather than an inflated balance. Committed watchlist spend of $15,510 falls entirely in the next three weeks.",
  "<strong>Two home closings would clear every gap in the window.</strong> Identified but unconfirmed sales total $109,500 across seven homes, none confirmed and none in the forecast. WW:3G at $2,000 has now been one document from closing for three consecutive weeks."
 ],
 "for_ownership": {
  "label": "Projected end-of-week cash",
  "number": 84926.04,
  "paragraph": "We close this week at roughly $84,900 available across all accounts. Only $5,800 of that is money leaving the business; the other $45,000 is the monthly distribution moving from the seven parks into Group Group. Golden Rule Practices is now overdrawn at the bank, and that is the item that needs attention this week. Cash across the portfolio has come down sharply over the last two weeks as a large backlog of pending payments finally cleared, which means the numbers now reflect real money rather than a lag. Looking out sixty days there are three weeks that go short unless a home closes, and we have seven homes worth about $110,000 in the sales pipeline with none confirmed yet."
